1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,615
This bell has been ringing since 1840...

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:04,443
on the same batteries.

3
00:00:04,768 --> 00:00:07,204
About ten billion rings, and nobody knows

4
00:00:07,204 --> 00:00:08,558
exactly what's inside them.

5
00:00:08,855 --> 00:00:09,992
It sits in a lab in Oxford.

6
00:00:10,419 --> 00:00:12,219
Two little brass bells, each on top of

7
00:00:12,219 --> 00:00:13,564
a tall dry battery.

8
00:00:13,861 --> 00:00:15,698
Between them hangs a metal ball, smaller

9
00:00:15,698 --> 00:00:16,398
than a pea.

10
00:00:16,679 --> 00:00:18,916
One bell charges it, pushes it away, the

11
00:00:18,916 --> 00:00:20,525
other bell pulls it in, and back again.

12
00:00:20,934 --> 00:00:22,034
Twice every second.

13
00:00:22,331 --> 00:00:24,095
It kept ringing through two world wars,

14
00:00:24,513 --> 00:00:26,231
the first planes, and the moon landing.

15
00:00:26,528 --> 00:00:27,746
But you can't hear it.

16
00:00:28,183 --> 00:00:29,756
It's sealed behind two layers of glass,

17
00:00:30,165 --> 00:00:32,037
and its batteries are coated in sulfur, so

18
00:00:32,037 --> 00:00:33,574
their recipe is still a mystery.

19
00:00:33,899 --> 00:00:35,589
One day the charge will run out.

20
00:00:36,299 --> 00:00:38,735
Until then... it just keeps ringing.
